WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.692
Hi, I’m Dan with Lakeland Surveying.

2
00:00:02.712 --> 00:00:04.155
For 50 years we’ve been
helping homeowners,

3
00:00:04.175 --> 00:00:08.276
builders and businesses across New Jersey know
exactly where their property starts and stops.

4
00:00:08.296 --> 00:00:12.255
People call us for all kinds of reasons,
but most of them come down to five.

5
00:00:12.275 --> 00:00:15.364
Number one: buying or selling a home.

6
00:00:15.384 --> 00:00:19.060
A survey shows your property lines,
where the house, fence and driveway sit,

7
00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.294
and whether anything
crosses a line it shouldn’t.

8
00:00:21.314 --> 00:00:25.441
Your attorney and title company use it to
make sure there are no surprises at closing.

9
00:00:25.461 --> 00:00:28.050
Number two: putting up a fence.

10
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.445
Many towns ask for a survey
with your fence permit.

11
00:00:30.465 --> 00:00:32.922
Even when they don’t,

12
00:00:32.942 --> 00:00:37.399
knowing exactly where the line is keeps
you from building on your neighbor’s side.

13
00:00:37.419 --> 00:00:39.434
Number three: building something.

14
00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:42.289
That could be an addition, a pool, a
deck, a garage or a brand-new home.

15
00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:44.730
Your town needs to see that
it meets setback rules,

16
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.251
and your builder needs it
staked out in the right spot.

17
00:00:47.271 --> 00:00:49.790
We handle both the plans and the stakeout.

18
00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.277
Number four: elevation certificates.

19
00:00:53.297 --> 00:00:57.418
If you’re in a flood zone, an elevation
certificate shows how high your home sits.

20
00:00:57.438 --> 00:01:01.045
It’s often needed for flood insurance
and for building or raising a home,

21
00:01:01.065 --> 00:01:03.035
and here in New Jersey that
covers a lot of homeowners.

22
00:01:03.055 --> 00:01:07.035
Number five: settling
property line questions.

23
00:01:07.055 --> 00:01:08.780
Maybe a neighbor’s shed looks too close,

24
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.211
or nobody’s sure where the
old fence really belongs.

25
00:01:11.231 --> 00:01:13.936
We research the deeds and
maps, measure in the field,

26
00:01:13.956 --> 00:01:16.885
and mark the actual corners so
everyone’s working from the facts.

27
00:01:16.905 --> 00:01:18.660
Whatever your project,

28
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.469
we’ve probably done it hundreds
of times over the last 50 years.

29
00:01:21.489 --> 00:01:26.148
Getting started is easy: fill out the quick
form on our website, or call or text us.

30
00:01:26.168 --> 00:01:29.289
We’ll get back to you
with answers and a quote.

31
00:01:29.309 --> 00:01:31.042
Thanks for watching.
